    "token_semantics": "Codex input_reported includes cached_input_tokens; uncached_input subtracts cache_read. Claude input_reported is uncached and excludes cache read and cache creation. Reasoning is a subset of output, not an additional token charge.",
    "latency": "Wall time includes CLI startup, model, tool calls and terminal completion. Codex memory call latency is the native MCP duration; Claude latency is elapsed time between native tool-use and tool-result timestamps.",
    "tool_counts": "Claude tool_use IDs are deduplicated; Codex completed native command/file/MCP events are counted. Codex catalog-discovery wrappers are reported separately, not added to nested tool counts. No matched baseline exists to attribute extra calls, tokens or latency to memory.",
    "quality": "Counts assess only directly observed eligible cases. Incorrect saves include unnecessary paraphrased duplicates and wrong scope for reusable findings, also separately classified; no factual inaccuracy was observed in those findings. Retrieval misses require an eligible record and include failure to invoke retrieval. Null means not evaluated, not zero. Record counts distinguish active, superseded and expired history, and separately record intended scopes.",
    "scope": "One observed sequence per policy/mode is evidence for these fixtures, not a reliability estimate. Unit and integration tests cover deterministic storage invariants separately. OpenCode and macOS/Linux live-agent behavior are not qualified by this report.",
    "cost": "No actual charge supplied; subscription and marginal memory cost remain unknown.",
    "raw_evidence": "Native transcripts and authenticated inspection snapshots remain in ignored temporary artifacts. This report contains no raw transcript, absolute path, run identifier or authentication material."
